Defense Evasion – BITSAdmin Download Investigation
1. Case Overview

Category: Defense Evasion
MITRE ATT&CK Technique: T1197 – BITS Jobs
Technique: BITSAdmin Download
Investigation Focus: Identification and analysis of BITSAdmin activity used to download and execute a file.

2. Investigation Objective

The objective of this investigation was to identify suspicious use of BITSAdmin for file transfer and determine whether any additional malicious activity occurred after the downloaded file was executed.

3. Investigation Methodology

Since the case was associated with BITSAdmin, the investigation was initiated by searching the available logs for the keyword:

bitsadmin

The investigation focused on identifying:

BITSAdmin execution.
Files downloaded using BITSAdmin.
The name and destination of the downloaded file.
Subsequent execution of the downloaded file.
Any additional activity following execution.
4. Investigation Findings

The investigation identified activity involving bitsadmin.exe.

BITSAdmin was observed downloading a file named:

T1197.md

The downloaded file was subsequently renamed to:

bitsadmin1_flag.ps1

The .ps1 extension indicates that the file was treated as a PowerShell script.

A subsequent search was performed for:

bitsadmin1_flag.ps1

This search was conducted to determine whether there was additional execution or related activity after the file was downloaded.

No further activity associated with bitsadmin1_flag.ps1 was observed in the available telemetry.

5. Attack Flow

The observed activity can be summarized as:

BITSAdmin (bitsadmin.exe)
↓
Downloads T1197.md
↓
File renamed to bitsadmin1_flag.ps1
↓
PowerShell script executed
↓
No further related activity observed

6. MITRE ATT&CK Mapping
MITRE ATT&CK	Technique	Observed Activity
T1197	BITS Jobs	bitsadmin.exe was used to download a file
T1059.001	PowerShell	The downloaded file was identified as a .ps1 script and executed

Note: The T1059.001 mapping should be retained only if the available logs provide evidence that PowerShell actually executed bitsadmin1_flag.ps1. The filename extension alone does not prove execution by PowerShell.

